---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

// Legal details of the data controller (as registered).
const controller = {
  name: 'Stefan Milić PR Grafički dizajn MIST Dizajn Studio',
  address: 'Stevana Sinđelića 109, 35208 Vojska, Serbia',
  registrationNumber: '67724160',
  taxId: '114623649',
};
const updated = '23 October 2026'; // update when the policy changes
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How MIST collects, uses and protects your personal data." hideCta>
  <article class="container legal">
    <h1 class="h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    <hr class="divider legal-rule" />

    <div class="body legal-body">
      <p>
        This policy explains what personal data MIST collects through mistdesign.co, why, and what you can do about it. It applies to everyone who visits
        the site, fills in The Gap Review brief, books a call or writes to me.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible for your data</h2>
      <p>
        {controller.name}<br />
        {controller.address}<br />
        Company registration number: {controller.registrationNumber}<br />
        Tax ID (PIB): {controller.taxId}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
      </p>
      <p>Throughout this policy, “MIST”, “I” and “me” refer to this business.</p>

      <h2>What I collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The Gap Review brief:</strong> your name, business name and business email, and, if you choose to share them, your phone or WhatsApp
          number, website or Instagram, and a link to files (for example WeTransfer). The brief also contains your answers about your business.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Emails:</strong> what you write to me, and my replies.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Booked calls:</strong> when you book a call through Calendly, Calendly collects your name, email and the time you choose, and shares them
          with me.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical data:</strong> my hosting provider records basic technical information, such as your IP address and browser, to keep the site
          secure and working.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Please don't include sensitive personal data (such as health information) in the brief. It isn't needed.</p>

      <h2>Why I use it, and on what basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>To prepare and send your Gap Review</strong>, confirm that your brief arrived, and follow up about the review and a possible project. This
          is a step you ask for before we may work together.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To send occasional emails from MIST</strong>, based on the consent you give in the brief. You can withdraw it at any time by replying
          “unsubscribe” or writing to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        </li>
        <li><strong>To answer your emails and prepare calls</strong> you book with me.</li>
        <li><strong>To measure how the site is used</strong> with Google Analytics, only with your consent to analytics cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>To keep the site secure</strong>, which is in the legitimate interest of both of us.</li>
        <li><strong>To meet legal obligations</strong>, such as accounting rules, if we work together.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>I don't sell your data, and I don't use it for automated decisions about you.</p>

      <h2>Who processes it for me</h2>
      <p>I use a few trusted services to run this site and my work. They process data on my behalf and only for these purposes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Netlify</strong> hosts the site and receives the brief form.</li>
        <li><strong>Google</strong> (Gmail and Google Sheets) stores the briefs and sends the confirmation email.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> measures how the site is used, only if you agree to analytics cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>GoDaddy</strong> provides my business email.</li>
        <li><strong>Calendly</strong> handles call bookings.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Some of these companies are based outside Serbia and the European Economic Area, mainly in the United States. In those cases, the transfer is
        protected by the safeguards the law requires, such as standard contractual clauses.
      </p>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>
        I keep your brief and our emails for as long as we're in touch about your review or a project, and no longer than three years after our last
        contact. If we work together, records needed for accounting are kept for as long as the law requires. You can ask me to delete your data sooner at
        any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>ask what data I hold about you, and get a copy of it;</li>
        <li>have it corrected or deleted;</li>
        <li>restrict or object to how I use it;</li>
        <li>receive it in a format you can take elsewhere;</li>
        <li>withdraw your consent to emails at any time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To use any of these rights, write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. I'll reply within 30 days. You can also file a complaint with
        the Commissioner for Information of Public Importance and Personal Data Protection of Serbia (<a
          href="https://www.poverenik.rs"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">poverenik.rs</a
        >), or, if you live in the EU, with your local data protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        mistdesign.co uses Google Analytics to see how many people visit, which pages they read and how they found the site, for example whether they
        sent a brief or booked a call. Google Analytics runs only if you click “Accept” in the cookie banner. If you decline, or don't choose, it isn't
        loaded and no analytics cookies are set.
      </p>
      <p>With your consent, Google Analytics sets these cookies:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>_ga</strong> and <strong>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</strong>: tell visits apart without identifying you by name. They expire after 13 months.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Analytics data is kept for 14 months. Google signals and advertising features are turned off, and the data isn't used for ads. Your choice is
        stored in your browser (not as a cookie), so the banner doesn't ask again. You can change it at any time with “Cookie settings” at the bottom of
        every page.
      </p>
      <p>The site uses no advertising cookies.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If I change how I handle your data, I'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-block: calc(var(--nav-h) + 120px) 160px;
    padding-left: var(--inset);
  }
  .legal > * {
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  .legal-updated {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--light-3);
  }
  .legal-rule {
    margin-top: 28px;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--dark-2);
  }
  .legal-body {
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .legal-body > * + * {
    margin-top: 17px;
  }
  .legal-body h2 {
    margin-top: 40px;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: normal;
    color: var(--light-1);
  }
  .legal-body h2 + * {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  .legal-body strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--light-1);
  }
  .legal-body ul {
    margin-block-end: 0;
    padding-left: 21px;
  }
  .legal-body li + li {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .legal-body a {
    color: var(--accent-3);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    transition: color 0.2s var(--ease);
  }
  @media (hover: hover) {
    .legal-body a:hover {
      color: var(--light-1);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 1079px) {
    .legal {
      padding-block: calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--space-lg)) var(--space-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
